# Folia Mobile — line ending policy.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to converting LF to CRLF on checkout, which corrupts
# patches/*.patch: `git am` rejects a patch whose context lines carry CRLF. The source tree is
# therefore pinned to LF, with the two Windows script types kept CRLF because that is what
# PowerShell and cmd expect when the file is opened or executed locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary payloads: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.7z binary
*.onnx binary
*.mp3 binary
